          <h1 class="about-title">Operator. Co-founder. Infrastructure leader.</h1>
        </header>

        <div class="about-body">
          <p>
            I build and operate production infrastructure, lead platform engineering teams, and run ventures. My work sits at the intersection of hands-on technical leadership and operational execution — the kind that involves both the architecture decision and the 2am incident call.
          </p>
          <p>
            I co-founded OUR+'R Technologies and run NullOrNaN Systems, a boutique advisory practice focused on reliability, platform engineering, and fractional CTO/COO work. I also built Reliability Lounge, a community and content hub for operators who work in production environments. Before that, I spent years at ASRC Federal leading infrastructure modernization across large, complex systems — cutting incident resolution time, improving platform stability, and building the kind of cross-functional operational discipline that doesn't get taught in a course.
          </p>
          <p>
            Right now I'm focused on seed-stage technical conversations, fractional leadership engagements, and growing the operator community around Reliability Lounge. I'm interested in the problems that don't have clean answers — the ones where engineering judgment and organizational trust matter as much as the tooling.
          </p>

          <p class="about-routing">
            If you want to work together, start at <a href="https://nullornan.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">nullornan.com</a>.
            If you want to connect, find me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/matthewcmcgowan" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>.
          </p>
